eleases/download/shared-p4-beta.2/SHA256SUMS.sig"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvucinozd/Pajoniiir/releases/assets/655641641","id":655641641,"node_id":"RA_kwDOS0ubjc4nFEwp","name":"SHA256SUMS.txt","label":"","uploader":{"login":"dvucinozd","id":58355393,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4MzU1Mzkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58355393?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvucinozd","html_url":"https://github.com/dvucinozd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvucinozd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvucinozd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvucinozd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvucinozd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvucinozd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvucinozd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvucinozd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvucinozd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvucinozd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"text/plain; charset=utf-8","state":"uploaded","size":1216,"digest":"sha256:786c8c72e5b71ec16f06e3ccb9820e6c02f91c4d05dd752a433f4238cd8a692b","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-10-19T08:07:41Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T08:07:41Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/dvucinozd/Pajoniiir/releases/download/shared-p4-beta.2/SHA256SUMS.txt"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvucinozd/Pajoniiir/tarball/shared-p4-beta.2","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvucinozd/Pajoniiir/zipball/shared-p4-beta.2","body":"One canonical P4 core; board-specific signed packages for **JC4880, JC1060 and M3**.\r\n\r\nThis is a **contributor beta / GitHub prerelease**. Stable **M2.5**, prior\r\nbeta1 assets and public OTA channels remain unchanged. No device is updated by\r\npublishing this release; M3/JC4880 acceptance below predates publication and\r\nbelongs to the exact, unchanged supplied bytes.\r\n\r\n## Changes since beta 1\r\n\r\n- Restore FLX4 headphone cue level: remove unintended12.041-dB transport\r\n  attenuation while retaining the legacy USB MAIN mirror behavior. Both M3 and\r\n  JC4880 bench listening/control checks are operator-confirmed. Start LEVEL low\r\n  after updating and raise gradually; this is not a new club-volume/electrical gate.\r\n- Re-anchor Master Tempo after ordinary-resampler fallback, fixing a reproduced\r\n  stale consumer-clock rewind (224 production-callback regression cases).\r\n- Apply the existing1-KiB task-context cache-maintenance bound to ordinary P4\r\n  builds. Range/alignment/error, ISR/critical delegation and full DMA ownership\r\n  semantics remain intact; bytes are bounded, not execution time guaranteed.\r\n- Remove unbounded largest-block heap walks from ordinary diagnostic snapshots.\r\n  Free/minimum counters remain measured; unavailable fragmentation/walk fields\r\n  are explicit null, not zero. Avoid resource walks and large logs during playback.\r\n- Include reviewed shared controller/lifecycle and JC1060 integration repairs,\r\n  plus DDJ-400 loop halve/double mappings. JC1060 physical gates remain open.\r\n\r\n## Downloads and exact identities\r\n\r\nThe distribution tag is a delivery record, not a common firmware build version.\r\nEach retained image has its own source SHA; production/test/tool/profile trees\r\nare identical. We deliberately avoid rebuilding accepted firmware just to make\r\nthe version strings match.\r\n\r\n| Board | Embedded version / source | Image bytes | Download |\r\n| --- | --- | ---: | --- |\r\n| JC4880 | `M2.5-249-g0a33ec1f` / `0a33ec1fb16c0136dccaa85ca63a6fbc00a4d527` | 2,609,952 | `jc4880-beta-kit.zip` or `main-deck-p4.ddjota` |\r\n| JC1060 | `M2.5-246-g2f2b0555` / `2f2b05558ccb68238d7228f59e52cd6c7d06e12f` | 2,668,480 | `jc1060-beta-kit.zip` or `main-deck-jc1060.ddjota` |\r\n| M3 | `M3-dev-g1556e8d7dfcb` / `1556e8d7dfcb4f016c52ab1a372dd2e076dcaa1f` | 2,603,312 | `m3-beta-kit.zip` or `main-deck-m3.ddjota` |\r\n\r\nMatching `*-debug.zip` files contain exact ELF/MAP/configuration. Kits include\r\nsigned OTA/manifest, raw application, board/configuration/lock identity, recovery\r\nbootloader/partition/otadata/flash metadata, module-specific notices and compiled\r\nprofiles. `controller-profiles.zip` provides the same six compiled fixtures;\r\nprofile availability does not imply hardware acceptance on every board.\r\n\r\nVerify SHA256SUMS and its detached signature, the signed release manifest and\r\neach kit inventory. Trusted public DER fingerprint:\r\n`125ef6eb776729e3018ecc564317254febec4a9a2bf34892e99d57f10bc02e43`.\r\nThe included public key alone does not establish trust. No private signing\r\nmaterial is included.\r\n\r\nStop both decks, keep power stable, and upload **only the matching board's\r\nsigned `.ddjota`**. Cross-board projects are not interchangeable. Raw BIN and\r\nthe kit's recovery/ contents are verified wired provisioning/recovery material,\r\nnot web OTA; check the actual layout and never erase the chip indiscriminately.\r\n\r\n- Ordinary **M3**: FLX4 USB2 FS/root1; storage USB3 HS/root0; PCM5102A MAIN48 kHz.\r\n  These assets do **not** use the experimental Hercules/S2 controller/storage\r\n  swap. Historical M3 `main-deck-p4` identity requires the preserving wired\r\n  migration before `main-deck-m3` OTA. M3-dev has no automatic pull discovery.\r\n- **JC4880**: controller root1/storage root0, PCM5102A MAIN with board-selected\r\n  rate (44.1 kHz with FLX4 in the accepted smoke).\r\n- **JC1060**: controller root0/storage root1, controller MAIN/cue and Ethernet;\r\n  no Wi-Fi or PCM5102A pin sharing. The kit identity supersedes historical\r\n  version numbers in its contributor handoff. First hardware tests are Kayrosen's\r\n  separate gate; this publication does not send him a message.\r\n\r\n## Validation and limits\r\n\r\n- **M3 supplied bytes**: installed VALID ota_1;100.264-s three-loop-exit replay,\r\n  30.145-s controls,60.133-s combined semantic checks, then3600.286 s /5301\r\n  samples of mixed-rate dual MT/loops. All22 strict deltas remain0. The operator\r\n  confirms clean MAIN/FLX4 headphones, fluid waveforms and stable display for\r\n  the full hour. Output-late24/max12,988 us includes a sample-observed3/60-s\r\n  cluster: investigation retained, **not zero-late or unrestricted reliability PASS**.\r\n- **JC4880 supplied bytes**: installed VALID ota_0;60.234 s /93 samples /1902\r\n  MIDI packets, all22 strict deltas0 and output-late0. Both loop/CUE transitions\r\n  and operator controls/PFL/MIX/LEVEL/audio/display confirmed. Long soak is\r\n  explicitly **waived / NOT RUN**, not PASS. The earlier0.076-s attempt was a\r\n  monitor-rate mismatch and remains archived as incomplete, not a firmware failure.\r\n- **JC1060 supplied bytes**: local IDF6.0.2 incremental build/board checks pass.\r\n  Physical installation/acceptance is **NOT RUN**, deferred to Kayrosen. Required\r\n  Ethernet/HTTP readiness/rollback, SD warm-reset, USB MAIN reconnect and listening\r\n  still require this exact image on real hardware.\r\n- Full host Qualification passed on identical production/test sources. Retained\r\n  IDF6.0.2 builds, unchanged dependency locks, single-BSP/project/source checks,\r\n  0x380000 budgets, signatures, matching ELF hashes, compiled fixtures and every\r\n  ZIP inventory verify. These are **retained incremental builds**, not new clean\r\n  release builds. Hosted CI is **NOT RUN (operator quota waiver)**.\r\n- Controls are exercised during playback, but observed input precedes automatic\r\n  loop exits. Sustained input pressure specifically through exit is not qualified.\r\n  Exact historical139-ms masking-call attribution and the late cluster stay open.\r\n- S2 remains **operator-closed with explicit waivers**; no further tests scheduled.\r\n  Historical S2/Hercules acceptance keeps its own image/topology scope and does\r\n  not qualify these ordinary M3 downloads. Wider controller LED/pad/FX, real\r\n  export/library, physical Campaign A and experimental feature gates stay partial\r\n  or NOT RUN. Recorder/alternate DJ UI and M3 Ethernet/Pro DJ Link stay experimental\r\n  or disabled in ordinary defaults. The entire shared-core acceptance is not closed.\r\n\r\nDistribution source: `d259a71ae716217a6448c374bf52c2c798d67ce8`. Per-board source commits are listed above and in the signed manifest.\r\n\r\n[OTA instructions](https://github.com/dvucinozd/Pajoniiir/blob/shared-p4-beta.2/docs/OTA-UPDATE.md) · [Board policies](https://github.com/dvucinozd/Pajoniiir/blob/shared-p4-beta.2/docs/SHARED_P4_BOARDS.md) · [Beta2 delivery record](https://github.com/dvucinozd/Pajoniiir/blob/shared-p4-beta.2/docs/validation/SHARED_P4_BETA_2_20261019.md) · [M3 hour evidence](https://github.com/dvucinozd/Pajoniiir/blob/shared-p4-beta.2/docs/validation/M3_MT_FALLBACK_HANDOFF_20261018.md) · [JC4880 smoke evidence](https://github.com/dvucinozd/Pajoniiir/blob/shared-p4-beta.2/docs/validation/M3_SOAK_CLOSEOUT_JC4880_OTA_20261019.md)\r\n"}